\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Charged Grassmann fields and an Abelian connection law}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{A charged lattice spinor couples to a connection by parallel transport. Its finite Grassmann integral changes the connection weight by a determinant and records ordered fermion insertions. Under which mass and symmetry conditions is that weight positive, and which charged observations survive gauge averaging?}

\p{The prerequisites are [paired Berezin coefficients](fdip-008F), the [covariant Dirac operator](fdip-009O), the [Wilson spacing convention](fdip-009U), and [path transport](fdip-006N). The construction passes from massive graded operators to exact source integration, then to finite vector identities and dressed observations. The final comparisons identify the classical Maxwell scaling and the hypotheses a fermionic transfer construction would require.}

